    "title": "Budget-three antipodal quotient pencil has a half-degree floor",
    "status": "PROVED",
    "closure": "proof",
    "statement": "In the antipodal quotient descent, let V span the unique degree-drop direction of the two-dimensional monic pencil and put r=d/4-1. Centering the four pencil parameters and reversing the quartic product identity at infinity proves deg V>=ceil((r-4)/2) whenever the characteristic exceeds d, improved to ceil((2r-4)/3) when the centered coefficient e_2 vanishes. On the maximal official row these are 2^36-2 and (2^38-4)/3 respectively.",
